  "marks": "Mastering: Presents a coherent directorial vision spanning both moments; specifies a staging configuration (e.g. thrust stage) and explains how it serves the dual-narrator direct address; names concrete lighting choices for the beach opening (e.g. a wide warm straw wash from overhead Fresnels, haze to suggest open air) and contrasts with the epilogue's isolated lighting special (e.g. single profile lantern, cold blue gel, tight focus on Sephy downstage centre); names specific sound choices (e.g. open ambient soundscape of waves and birdsong for the opening, giving way to silence or a sustained low underscore for the epilogue); explains how performer positioning (proxemics, levels) reinforces the isolation of the final moment; all choices are anchored to named dramatic moments and justified with reference to audience effect and the play's themes.\n\nSecure: Addresses both moments with mostly concrete design choices; includes at least one named lighting element and one sound element; explains the effect on the audience; staging configuration is mentioned if not fully justified.\n\nDeveloping: Addresses one moment more fully than the other; design choices are sometimes generic ('dark lighting for the sad ending'); effect on audience is implied rather than stated.\n\nEmerging: Lists some design ideas without relating them to the specific moments or explaining effects; response is largely descriptive."
 }
]

